{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.preludes.md | sed -n '510,727p'\"","aggregated_output":"   510\t| `[1, 2]` | cell `{:py/type :list :items [1 2]}` | persistent vector `[1 2]` |\n   511\t| `(1, 2)` | `{:py/type :tuple :items [1 2]}` | persistent vector `[1 2]` |\n   512\t| `{\"a\": 1}` | cell `{:py/type :dict ...}` | persistent map `{\"a\" 1}` |\n   513\t| `{1, 2}` | cell `{:py/type :set ...}` | persistent set `#{1 2}` |\n   514\t| `def f(x): ...` | cell `{:py/type :function :code (fn [args] ...) :yang.call/entry ...}` | authenticated cell `{:clj.py/type :function :name s :spec spec :yang.call/entry ...}` |\n   515\t| Truthiness | `0`, `\"\"`, `[]`, `{}`, `None`, `False` falsy | Clojure truthiness (`clj.py/truthy`): only `nil` and `false` falsy (`0`, `\"\"`, `[]` are truthy) |\n   516\t| Equality `==` / `!=` | `1 == 1.0 == True`, structural list/dict | Recursive kind-strict equality (`clj.py/eq`): `1 == 1` `true`, `1 == 1.0` `false`, `1 == True` `false`, `NaN == NaN` `false`, `0.0 == -0.0` `true`, recursive over persistent collections |\n   517\t\n   518\t*Truth-in-advertising invariant:* `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` explicitly declares Clojure truthiness, persistent immutable collections, non-numeric booleans, and kind-strict equality as its support profile — never CPython parity.\n   519\t\n   520\t### 7.2 Portable numeric contract (`clj.py` over `yin.vm.integer` + `yrt.float` + `yrt.int`)\n   521\t\n   522\tPer `yang.antlr.md` §8.5.5, raw `+`, `-`, `*`, `/`, `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=` on decoded `data/float64` carriers are **not portable across Node/JVM/Dart**. Furthermore, `yin.vm.data/data-number?` (`src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc:418`) recognizes host numbers and exact-integer carriers, **not** CLJS `Float64` carriers (`src/cljc/dao/host/number.cljc:76`).\n   523\t\n   524\t**Host prerequisite (`data/float64?`):** `yin.vm.data` adds one `:pure` unary export **`data/float64?`** backed directly by existing `dao.jing.cbor/float64?` (`src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:212` — already implemented for JVM `Double`/`Float`, Dart `double`, JS `Float64`/non-integral/non-finite/`-0.0` `Number`, and Jolt Scheme flonums). Like owner decision A12.6 in `yang.typescript.md`, adding a new export to `yin.vm.data` changes no existing `py`/`js`/`php`/`clj` manifest or golden address because existing profiles do not read it; `data/float64?` is an explicit prerequisite of P3 (and optional for P1).\n   525\t\n   526\tTherefore, `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` routes ALL arithmetic, floor division, remainder, power, comparisons, and equality through `clj.py/*` adapters requiring host `integer` (`:min-bits 53`) and `data` (with `data/float64?`):\n   527\t\n   528\t1. **Portable kind classification (`clj.py/num-kind`):**\n   529\t   ```clojure\n   530\t   (if (integer/integer? x)\n   531\t     :int\n   532\t     (if (data/float64? x) :float :other))\n   533\t   ```\n   534\t   `true`/`false`, `nil`, strings, symbols, keywords, collections, callables, and cells all answer `:other` cleanly across all four hosts (`integer/integer?` at `src/cljc/yin/vm/integer.cljc:595`). Non-numeric operands raise guest error `{:clj.py/error :type-error ...}` (in `v1`, string `+` concatenates via `data/str-concat`; `*` is strictly numeric).\n   535\t2. **Int × Int:**\n   536\t   - `+`, `-`, `*`, `//`, `%`, `**` (`e >= 0`), `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`: execute through `integer/add`, `integer/sub`, `integer/mul`, `integer/floor-div-mod`, `integer/pow`, `integer/compare`, filtering results through `yrt.int/check-limit` (translating `:yin.vm.integer/bit-limit`, `:digit-limit`, `:float-overflow` to guest error maps via `clj/raise`, never catching operational host throws). Check `b == 0` **before** `integer/floor-div-mod` or `integer/true-div` to raise a guest zero-division error rather than an operational throw.\n   537\t   - `/`: checks `b != 0`, calls `integer/true-div`, filters via `yrt.int/check-limit`, and boxes as `data/float64`.\n   538\t   - `**` with negative integer exponent `e < 0`: if `a == 0` raises guest zero-division error; otherwise converts **only base `a`** via `(data/float64 (yrt.int/check-limit (integer/to-float a) ...))` and calls `(yrt.float/neg-pow-result base-boxed (integer/neg e) :half)` passing the **exact positive integer magnitude** `(integer/neg e)` (never converting `e` to float!). If `yrt.float/neg-pow-result` returns `:yrt.float/underflow`, `clj.py` raises guest overflow error `{:clj.py/error :overflow ...}` outside any raw-double leaf frame.\n   539\t3. **Float × Float and Mixed Int × Float:**\n   540\t   - Exact int operands promote via `(data/float64 (yrt.int/check-limit (integer/to-float i) ...))`.\n   541\t   - **`//` (`clj.py/float-floordiv`):** zero divisor raises guest zero-division error; NaN in either operand or `Inf // Inf` returns boxed `yrt.float/nan`; `±Inf // finite` returns signed `±Inf`; `finite // ±Inf` returns boxed `-1.0` when signs differ (and `finite != 0`) else boxed `zero-like`; finite operands compute exact quotient `q = (- (/ (- x m) y) adjust)` inside a leaf frame, floor via `yrt.float/floor-int-result` (passing the quotient directly as boxed float when `:yrt.float/out-of-range` since `|q| >= 2^53` is already integral), and return `data/float64`.\n   542\t   - **`%` (`clj.py/float-mod`):** guards ALL preconditions before ever reaching `yrt.float/fmod-pos`:\n   543\t     - Zero divisor (`y == 0.0`): raises guest zero-division error.\n   544\t     - NaN in either operand, or non-finite `x` (`±Inf`): returns boxed `yrt.float/nan`.\n   545\t     - Finite `x`, infinite `y` (`±Inf`): handled directly without `fmod-pos` — returns `zero-like(y)` when `x == 0.0`, `x` when `x` and `y` share sign, and `y` (`±Inf`) when signs oppose (floored modulo).\n   546\t     - Finite `x`, finite nonzero `y`: calls `m0 = (yrt.float/fmod-pos (abs x) (abs y))` inside a pure leaf frame, restores dividend sign `m`, converts `m == 0.0` to `zero-like(y)`, sign-corrects `m` toward `y`, and returns `data/float64`.\n   547\t   - **`**` (`clj.py/float-pow`):**\n   548\t     - `y == 0.0`: returns boxed `data/float64 1.0`; NaN in either operand (after `y == 0.0`): returns boxed `yrt.float/nan`; infinite `y` (`±Inf`): explicitly refuses with guest error `{:clj.py/error :unsupported-op :op :pow-infinite}` (matching `php/pow-float:1391`).\n   549\t     - Finite `y`: checks exact integrality via `(let [e (integer/from-float y)] (= (integer/compare-float e y) 0))`:\n   550\t       - Integral `e >= 0`: computes `yrt.float/fpow-half-raw` inside a leaf frame and reboxes `data/float64`;\n   551\t       - Integral `e < 0`: if `x == 0.0` raises guest zero-division error, else delegates boxed `x` and exact positive integer `(integer/neg e)` to `yrt.float/neg-pow-result` (mapping `:yrt.float/underflow` to guest overflow error outside the leaf frame);\n   552\t       - **Fractional exponent** (`compare-float != 0`): explicitly refuses with guest error `{:clj.py/error :unsupported-op :op :pow-fractional}` (matching `js/pow-fractional:650` and `php/pow-float:1400`, known gap `G-pow-frac`).\n   553\t   - **Mixed ordering (`<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=`):** if either operand is NaN answers `false`; Float × Float unwraps inside a pure leaf helper; Int × Float / Float × Int compares via exact `integer/compare-float` (never rounding large ints to float!).\n   554\t4. **Recursive portable equality (`clj.py/eq`, `clj.py/ne`):**\n   555\t   - Never delegates collections containing floats to host Yin `=`, because CLJS `Float64.-equiv` (`src/cljc/dao/host/number.cljc:98–101`) equates `NaN` with `NaN` and distinguishes `-0.0` from `0.0` — violating IEEE scalar equality inside `[NaN] == [NaN]` or `[0.0] == [-0.0]`.\n   556\t   - `clj.py/eq` therefore recurses explicitly:\n   557\t     - `:int` × `:int`: `(= (integer/compare a b) 0)`.\n   558\t     - `:float` × `:float`: leaf unwrap → `false` if either is NaN, else `(= ax bx)` (`+0.0 == -0.0` is `true`, `NaN == NaN` is `false` on all 4 hosts).\n   559\t     - `:int` × `:float` (or vice versa): **`false`** (kind-strict Clojure equality: `1 != 1.0`).\n   560\t     - Vectors / sequential collections (`data/vector?`, `clojure.core/sequential?`): equal count + pairwise recursive `clj.py/eq`.\n   561\t     - Maps (`data/map?`, excluding authenticated cell-refs): `clj.py/map-from` (and `get-item`) normalizes `-0.0` float keys to `+0.0`; `clj.py/eq` compares count and matches entries by converting to entry pairs and checking each key/value pair recursively via `clj.py/eq` (so `{\"a\": -0.0} == {\"a\": 0.0}` is `true` and `{NaN: 1} == {NaN: 1}` is `false` uniformly across all 4 hosts, even if a collection originated outside `clj.py`).\n   562\t     - Sets (`kind/set?`): `clj.py/set-from` normalizes `-0.0` elements to `+0.0`; `clj.py/eq` compares count and checks every element membership recursively via `clj.py/eq` (so `#{0.0} == #{-0.0}` is `true` and `#{NaN} == #{NaN}` is `false` on all 4 hosts).\n   563\t     - Other scalars (`nil`, booleans, strings, keywords, symbols, authenticated cell-refs): host `=`.\n   564\t\n   565\t### 7.3 Python lowering Hook ABI & `clj.py` adapters\n   566\t\n   567\tRather than pretending `clj/*` shares identical signatures with `py/*`, the frontend keeps its fixed **Python Lowering Hook ABI** (`yang.python.antlr.contract`) and `clj.py` implements every hook with compatible arity and semantics:\n   568\t\n   569\t| Hook key | Frontend ABI signature | `clj.py` implementation |\n   570\t|---|---|---|\n   571\t| `:env/local-get` | `[cell name]` | Reads `(cell/get cell)`; raises guest unbound error if `:clj/unbound` (supporting parameter init, local reassignment, and `nonlocal` via shared lexical cells when `:mutation/locals :cell`). |\n   572\t| `:env/global-get` | `[globals-cell name]` | Reads the unit's **per-module** `globals-cell` first; on miss, falls back to `clj.py`'s explicit `:ambient-projections` lookup table; on miss there, raises guest `NameError`-equivalent map `{:clj.py/error :name-error :name name}`. Keeps distinct compiled modules isolated instead of sharing one flat `clj.rt/globals` map. |\n   573\t| `:env/global-set` | `[globals-cell name value]` | Writes `(cell/set! globals-cell (assoc (cell/get globals-cell) name value))` and returns `value`. |\n   574\t| `:fn/make` | `[fname spec defaults kwdefaults code]` | Accepts the exact 5 arguments from `yang.python.antlr.lower/function-value:1870` (lowering already refused defaults/kwonly/kwstar/kwargs when disabled); mints an **authenticated task-heap cell** (`§7.4`). |\n   575\t| `:fn/call` | `[callee args]` | Checks `clj.py/admitted-callable?` first (`§7.4`), then routes to `yang.call/invoke` with `clj.py`'s condition-unwrapping / provenance-retaining raise exit, never bare `clj/raise`. |\n   576\t| `:ctrl/try` | `[body handler orelse]` | **3-arg signature** calling `yrt.escape/try-orelse` on `(clj/rt-ctx)`, preserving Python `try` / `except` / `else`. |\n   577\t| `:ctrl/try-finally` | `[body fin]` | Calls `yrt.escape/try-finally` on `(clj/rt-ctx)` with `normal-arg = nil`. |\n   578\t| `:ctrl/raise` | `[e]` | Calls `clj/raise` (delegating to `yrt.escape/raise` on `(clj/rt-ctx)`). |\n   579\t| `:ctrl/call-ec` | `[f]` | Calls `yrt.escape/call-ec` on `(clj/rt-ctx)` with `normal-arg = nil`. |\n   580\t| `:ctrl/for-each` | `[iterable step-fn]` | Iterates `(clojure.core/seq iterable)` via `first`/`rest`, invoking `step-fn` per element (supports `break`/`continue` via `call-ec` and eager comprehensions). |\n   581\t| `:unit/run-main` | `[body-fn]` | Calls `(clj/init!)` and `(clojure.core/init!)`; allocates a **fresh per-unit `globals` cell** (`(cell/new {})`) and `globals-fn`; invokes `(body-fn globals globals-fn)` inside a top-level handler; returns the value **verbatim without stripping `[:yin.k/ok ...]`** so ordinary Python data shaped like `[:yin.k/ok 42]` passes through uncorrupted. |\n   582\t\n   583\t*(Lowerings with `:mutation/locals :single-assignment` remain a separate, stricter profile variant that omits `cell/new`/`cell/set!` and refuses assignment/reassignment to locals, loops with mutated accumulators, and `nonlocal`.)*\n   584\t\n   585\t### 7.4 Cross-unit callable admission, source authority, and §8.10.7 exception bridging\n   586\t\n   587\tBecause `yang.call/eligible?` (`src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc:29–48`) only dereferences authenticated cell-refs and leaves ordinary maps intact, structural eligibility alone does **not** stop source-constructed maps carrying `:yang.call/entry` from masquerading as callables when source maps are first-class data. Likewise, as `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1280–1306` and `2400–2424` show, immutable Clojure descriptors carry a unit-local `:clj/admission` witness closing over that unit's private `dsg__call_token` rather than cross-unit admission, whereas **authenticated task-heap cells** (`cell/authentic?`, `clojure.cljc:2400–2408`) are admitted across **every** independently compiled unit (`yang.clojure`, `clojure.core`, `clj.py`, `py`, `js`, `php`).\n   588\t\n   589\tTherefore `clj.py` enforces the full §8.10 + §8.10.7 contract:\n   590\t\n   591\t1. **Source-level callable admission (`clj.py/admitted-callable?`):**\n   592\t   - Called by `clj.py/call` and source-facing callable predicates (`clj.py/callable?`, and standalone `clojure.core/fn?`) **before** invoking `yang.call/invoke`:\n   593\t     ```clojure\n   594\t     (and (data/map? x)\n   595\t          (= (get x :type) :cell-ref)\n   596\t          (cell/authentic? x)\n   597\t          (data/callable? (yang.call/entry x))\n   598\t          (yang.call/eligible? x))\n   599\t     ```\n   600\t   - Any plain source map (including `{:yang.call/entry ...}`) or unauthenticated `{:type :cell-ref ...}` map fails `clj.py/admitted-callable?` immediately; `clj.py/call` mints a retained `:yang.call/not-callable` protocol condition via private `cell/dsg__new-provenance` and raises it via `clj/raise`, never calling `yang.call/invoke` on forged source data.\n   601\t   - Preserves zero-wrapper function identity (`=`) across all cell-backed frontends (`py`, `js`, `php`, `clj.py`, standalone `clojure.core`). Note the explicit boundary: foreign immutable non-cell descriptors (such as legacy unit-local `yang.clojure` descriptors) are not admitted as raw maps in `clj.py` unless constructed as authenticated cell-backed descriptors (as standalone `clojure.core` does in §7.5), avoiding receiver-side replacement wrappers (`yang.antlr.md` §8.10.2).\n   602\t2. **Trusted cell-backed callable constructor (`clj.py/make-fn`):**\n   603\t   - Allocates `(cell/new {:clj.py/type :function, :name fname, :spec spec, :yang.call/entry entry})`.\n   604\t3. **Value-returning entry boundary inside `:yang.call/entry` (with binding inside the boundary):**\n   605\t   - **Protocol record check (outside try):** validates `(yang.call/valid-invocation? invocation)`; a malformed protocol record transfers `:yang.call/invalid-invocation` directly via `yang.call/transfer`.\n   606\t   - **Value-returning boundary (`yrt.escape/try-value` — NOT `try-orelse`!):** installs the exception handler on `(clj/rt-ctx)` **before** parameter binding so binding and body execution share one cleanup/catch boundary (mirroring `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1244–1256` and `yang.antlr.md:3861–3867` §8.10.7):\n   607\t     - Inside `try-value`: checks empty `:yang.call/named` (when `:calls/kwargs :refused`) and positional/varargs arity against `:spec`, raising local `clj.py` binding exceptions via `clj/raise` so callee binding errors are delivered to the caller under **`:yang.call/thrown`** per §8.10.7; then evaluates `(body-fn bound-args)`.\n   608\t     - On normal completion, `yrt.escape/try-value` restores `(clj/rt-ctx)` and returns the body's value verbatim (`20` in §7.6).\n   609\t     - On escape with `e`, the handler inspects private `(cell/dsg__provenance e)`: if non-nil (an authentic retained protocol condition from a deeper cross-language boundary), forwards that retained condition **directly** to `(get invocation :yang.call/raise)` without double-wrapping; otherwise wraps `e` (including condition-shaped user maps!) via `(yang.call/thrown e)` and transfers it to `(get invocation :yang.call/raise)`.\n   610\t4. **Call-site boundary (`clj.py/call`):**\n   611\t   - Passes a dedicated `raise-exit` closure to `yang.call/invoke`:\n   612\t     - If `(= (get condition :yang.call/reason) :yang.call/thrown)`, calls `(clj/raise (get condition :yang.call/value))` (unwrapping user-thrown values identically to `clojure.cljc:1441–1447`).\n   613\t     - Otherwise retains the protocol condition inside a private provenance carrier `(clj/raise (cell/dsg__new-provenance condition condition))` (mirroring `clojure.cljc:1448–1450`), preserving full condition fidelity across A → B → A unwinds and `finally` blocks.\n   614\t   - `cell/dsg__new-provenance` and `cell/dsg__provenance` remain strictly private inside trusted Layer-2b `clj.py` (`module-uast` only), never exported or exposed to `yrt.*` or source scope.\n   615\t\n   616\t### 7.5 Portable `clojure.core` linked library contract\n   617\t\n   618\tIn Slice P3, `clojure.core` is published as an **explicit, standalone, portable linker module** (`clojure.core`) requiring `yang.call`, `clj`, `yrt.escape`, `yrt.float`, and `yrt.int`, and registered against host modules `kind`, `data` (with `data/float64?`), `integer` (`:min-bits 53`), and `cell` (strictly omitting host-dependent exports):\n   619\t\n   620\t1. **Portable subset and numeric/equality adaptations (`yang.clojure/library` base + portable rewrites):**\n   621\t   - Exported non-numeric definitions retained from `yang.clojure/library`: `identity`, `second`, `boolean?`, `update`, `count`, `contains?`, `symbol?`, `keyword?`, `meta`, `name`, `symbol`, `keyword`, `str`, `fresh-symbol`, `gensym`, `last`, `butlast`, `string?`, `with-meta`, `coll?`, `vector?`, `map?`, `set?`, `sequential?`, `seq?`, `list?`, `rest`, `seq`, `reverse`, `cons`, `list`, `vector`, `reduced`, `reduced?`, `unreduced`, `reduce`, `map`, `mapv`, `filter`, `remove`, `into`, `concat`, `keys`, `vals`, `disj`, `union`, `difference`, `merge`, `comp`, `partial`.\n   622\t   - **Portable numeric & equality rewrites (strictly inside standalone `clojure.core`, leaving default `yang.clojure` untouched):**\n   623\t     - `inc` and `dec`: route through portable numeric dispatch (`integer/integer?` → `integer/add`/`integer/sub` + `yrt.int/check-limit`; `data/float64?` → leaf unwrap ± `1.0` + `data/float64`; non-numeric → guest type error via `clj/throw`), never bare VM `+`/`-` (`yin.vm.cljc:404`).\n   624\t     - `rem`: checks `(and (integer/integer? a) (integer/integer? b))` and `b != 0` (raising guest errors otherwise), computes `(data/nth (integer/quot-rem a b) 1)`, and checks `yrt.int/check-limit`.\n   625\t     - `not=`: delegates to portable recursive equality (§7.2: exact `integer/compare`, unwrapped float `-0.0 == 0.0` / `NaN != NaN`, kind-strict `1 != 1.0`, recursive collection equality), never leaking CLJS `Float64.-equiv`.\n   626\t     - `int?`: delegates to `integer/integer?` (consistent exact-integer answer across all 4 hosts, including JS/Dart big integers).\n   627\t     - `nth`: validates index via `integer/integer?`.\n   628\t     - `fn?`: checks `clj.py`-equivalent authenticated cell admission (`(and (data/map? x) (= (get x :type) :cell-ref) (cell/authentic? x) (data/callable? (yang.call/entry x)) (yang.call/eligible? x))`, or `(data/callable? x)` only for primitive/VM closures, never plain maps).\n   629\t   - **Explicitly excluded for 4-host portability:** `var?` (CLJ-only in `kind-module:2593`) and `resolve` (`kind/resolve` absent from `kind-module`).\n   630\t2. **Newly authored portable helpers & primitive callable projections (not pre-existing in `yang.clojure/library`):**\n   631\t   - Pure guest additions in `clojure.core`: `assoc-in`, `update-in`, `get-in`, `hash-map`, `set`.\n   632\t   - **Primitive callable projections:** thin cell-backed callable wrappers over VM primitives (`nil?`, `empty?`, `not`, `first`, `conj`, `assoc`, `get`, `vec`) so Python source can either call `is_empty(xs)` directly OR pass `is_empty` as a higher-order callback to `filter`/`map`.\n   633\t3. **Uniform cell-backed callable construction (exports AND dynamically returned closures) & reconciled call path:**\n   634\t   - **Every** exported AND dynamically returned function in standalone `clojure.core` — both top-level functions allocated in `(clojure.core/init!)` **AND** closures returned at runtime by `comp`, `partial`, or higher-order helpers — is constructed via a single cell-backed constructor `(cell/new {:clojure.core/type :function :yang.call/entry entry})` using the same `yrt.escape/try-value` §8.10.7 entry bridge.\n   635\t   - **Reconciled internal call path:**\n   636\t     - Static sibling calls within `clojure.core` (e.g., `map` calling internal `seq`, `first`, `rest`, `cons`, `reverse`) invoke stripped internal module lambdas directly (zero allocation, immune to caller global redefinition).\n   637\t     - Dynamic calls to user-supplied closures (`f` in `map`, `filter`, `remove`, `reduce`, `update`, `comp`, `partial`) go through standalone `clojure.core`'s dynamic call helper, which validates authenticated cell admission (`cell/authentic?` + `data/callable?` entry + `yang.call/eligible?`) and invokes `yang.call/invoke` with the §8.10.7 exception bridge — **never** using `yang.clojure`'s map-only `[dsg__call_token args]` shortcut (`clojure.cljc:2432`). Returned closures from `comp`/`partial` keep identical cell identity across every independently compiled frontend unit with zero receiver-side replacement wrappers.\n   638\t4. **No implicit namespace dump & zero impact on default `yang.clojure` in P3:**\n   639\t   - Adding `'clojure.core` to `:requires` exposes nothing to user code on its own; only explicit entries in `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections` enter source scope.\n   640\t   - Existing `yang.clojure`'s `library-for` bundling stays untouched in P3 so default Clojure compilation keeps zero golden churn; migrating `yang.clojure` itself onto `clojure.core` is scheduled separately (owner decision D6).\n   641\t\n   642\t### 7.6 Concrete lowering example\n   643\t\n   644\t```python\n   645\tdef sum_even_squares(xs):\n   646\t    if is_empty(xs):\n   647\t        return 0\n   648\t    evens = filter(lambda n: n % 2 == 0, xs)\n   649\t    squares = map(lambda n: n * n, evens)\n   650\t    return reduce(lambda a, b: a + b, 0, squares)\n   651\t```\n   652\t\n   653\t- `is_empty` resolves (below lexical/module scope) via `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections` to `clojure.core`'s projected `empty?` cell-backed callable.\n   654\t- `filter`, `map`, `reduce` resolve to `clojure.core`'s task-instantiated cell-backed callables.\n   655\t- `%`, `*`, `+`, `==` lower hygienically to `clj.py/mod`, `clj.py/mul`, `clj.py/add`, `clj.py/eq` (exact `yin.vm.integer` / `yrt.float` paths).\n   656\t- `lambda n: ...` lowers to `clj.py/make-fn`, producing an authenticated cell-backed `yang.call` callable invoked directly by `clojure.core/filter` and `clojure.core/map`.\n   657\t- `sum_even_squares([1, 2, 3, 4])` evaluates `[1 2 3 4]` → `20` (exact persistent integer), and returns `20` unchanged (not unwrapped by `[:yin.k/ok ...]`).\n   658\t\n   659\t---\n   660\t\n   661\t## 8. Portability, content addressing, and malleability\n   662\t\n   663\t### 8.1 Multi-host portability (JVM, CLJS/Node, CLJD/Dart, Jolt/Scheme)\n   664\t\n   665\tAll new `yang.core.*` and `yang.rt.*` (`yrt.*`) namespaces live in `src/cljc/` and obey the repository's four-host constraints:\n   666\t- **ClojureDart AOT literal limits:** Consolidate `defquoted` (`yang.python.antlr.prelude`, `yang.typescript.antlr.prelude`, `yang.php.antlr.quoted`) into `yang.core.prelude/defquoted`, keeping identical `:cljs`/`:cljd` macro imports, reader aliases, and EDN expansion.\n   667\t- **No bare integral float literals & safe integer bounds:** `yrt.float` and `clj.py` construct every float constant via `data/float-value`/`data/float64`, `-0.0` via `(* (data/float-value -1) (data/float-value 0))`, and avoid integer literals past `2^53 - 1`.\n   668\t- **Canonical ordering (`b86bc0e8` invariant):** Recipes, profiles, descriptor maps, and emitted UAST operand sequences sort keys deterministically (`sort-by str` / explicit vector order) and never iterate host maps when building AST nodes, guaranteeing byte-identical `dao.jing.cbor` hashes across JVM, Node, Dart, and Jolt.\n   669\t- **No JVM-only reflection:** `yang.core.semantics` and `yang.core.prelude` use pure portable Clojure data transforms with zero `eval`, runtime `tools.reader`, or JVM reflection.\n   670\t\n   671\t### 8.2 Dependency graph and malleability (`docs/agents/malleability.md`)\n   672\t\n   673\tPreserves a strictly layered, cycle-free dependency graph verified with `clj ./bin/analyze-deps.clj`:\n   674\t\n   675\t```text\n   676\tLayer A (AST & Data Schemas):    yang.core.uast\n   677\tLayer B (Pure Composition):      yang.core.prelude, yang.core.semantics\n   678\tLayer C (Registry Admission):    yang.core.prelude-admission, yang.core.module, yang.core.publication\n   679\tLayer D (Shared Guest Modules):  yang.core.call, yang.rt.escape, yang.rt.float, yang.rt.int\n   680\tLayer E (Language Frontends):    yang.python.antlr.*, yang.typescript.antlr.*, yang.php.antlr.*, yang.clojure.*\n   681\t```\n   682\t\n   683\t- **Frontend isolation:** Frontend-specific hook ABI contracts (like `yang.python.antlr.contract`) remain in Layer E, never in `yang.core.*`.\n   684\t- **Bounded public APIs:** Host namespaces maintain 2–5 `defn` entry points (`yang.core.semantics`: `validate-descriptor`, `capability-status`, `literal-node`, `hook-symbol`, `resolve-ambient`), and guest `yrt.*` modules bound their public export count cleanly (grouping only cohesive primitives per module rather than creating a sprawling grab-bag).\n   685\t\n   686\t### 8.3 Content-addressing and golden migration discipline\n   687\t\n   688\t1. **Address-neutral slices (P0, P2, P3):** `P0` preserves exact pre-change UAST bytes on frozen snapshots; `P2` emits byte-identical UAST for every default language profile; `P3` adds `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` and `clojure.core` without changing `yang.clojure`'s default `library-for` output or any existing language goldens.\n   689\t2. **One batched profile bump (`P1`):** Each `yrt.*` module (`yrt.escape`, `yrt.float`, `yrt.int`) is implemented and validated independently first, then activated across `py`, `js`, `php`, and `clj` in one coordinated profile bump so `:segment/blake3-*` goldens (`scanner_goldens.cljc`, `float_address_test.cljc`, `dht-import-v1.edn`, `clojure_callsite_test.cljc`, linked harnesses) refresh once.\n   690\t\n   691\t---\n   692\t\n   693\t## 9. Phased implementation roadmap and acceptance gates\n   694\t\n   695\t| Slice | Scope & deliverables | Golden impact | Concrete acceptance gate |\n   696\t|---|---|---|---|\n   697\t| **P0 — Composition plumbing & `defquoted` consolidation** | Consolidate `defquoted` into `yang.core.prelude`; implement `:yang.prelude/recipe` / `:yang.prelude/profile` composition and verified-closure validation in `yang.core.prelude` + `prelude-admission` (preserving operand sequencing, `init!` placement, tail marking, `:linear`/`:balanced` mode, and Clojure's custom preamble). | **Zero** (byte-identical emission) | Compare generated UAST/specs against frozen pre-change snapshots of `py`/`js`/`php`/`clj`/`yang.call`; test verified-closure edge validation, missing transitive artifact/export refusal, provenance-door/effect-ceiling exclusions, and projected-name collision refusal. |\n   698\t| **P1 — Layer 2a Tier 1 (`yrt.escape`, `yrt.float`, `yrt.int`)** | Implement the three stateless guest modules (frame indexing via `data/nth`, status-returning `yrt.float` boxed boundaries with zero raw-double callbacks); migrate `js`/`clj` from 4-slot to 5-slot contexts (`:handlers :depth :base :frame`); preserve open non-`:finally` (`:generator`) boundary dispatch; add `dsg__add`/`dsg__lte` guest helpers for bundled `clj`; activate across `py`, `js`, `php`, `clj` in one coordinated bump. | **One batched bump** | Unit tests for `yrt.*` on semantic/stack/register VMs; bundled/linked `yang.clojure` parity with source-defined `(defn get ...)` and active nested `try`/`throw`/`finally` frames; existing Python & PHP generator tests green; 4→5-slot migration tests; PHP `abandon-to` / `call-terminal` & normal `finally` replacement (`:py/None`, `:js/undefined`, `:php/null`, `nil`); `1.1 ** 6` bit-pattern parity (`fpow-half` vs `fpow-base`); exceptional `yrt.float` underflow/out-of-range status returns (`2.0 ** -2000`, `floor(1e30)`, `floor(NaN)`, `floor(Inf)`) under `%capture`/safepoints across 4 hosts; `yin.vm.integer` v4 three-reason translation without masking operational throws; independent concurrent `py`/`js`/`php`/`clj` tasks sharing `yrt.*`; bundled == linked + 4-host + CPython/Node/PHP oracle parity; `clj ./bin/analyze-deps.clj` clean. |\n   699\t| **P2 — Lowering parameterization (`yang.core.semantics` + frontend contracts)** | Implement generic `yang.core.semantics`; define `yang.python.antlr.contract` (then TS/PHP); refactor `yang.python.antlr.lower` to read literals/hooks/capabilities/projections from `:yang.semantics/descriptor` defaulting to `:yang.python/py-v1`. | **Zero** (byte-identical default output) | Byte-for-byte UAST equality test across the full corpus under `:yang.python/py-v1`; tests covering every supported lowering path and capability mode (`:cell`, `:single-assignment`, `:ambient-only`), unqualified-hook rejection, reserved-door projection ban, and explicit refusal of generator expressions when `:control/generators :refused`. |\n   700\t| **P3 — `clojure.core` prelude for `yang.python` (`:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`)** | Add `:pure` `data/float64?` to `yin.vm.data`; publish standalone portable `clojure.core` module (`§7.5` with cell-backed dynamic closures & portable `inc`/`dec`/`rem`/`not=`) + `clj.py` adapter + `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` descriptor; leave `yang.clojure`'s default `library-for` untouched; wire `yang.frontend` multi-revision catalog selection. | **Zero** on existing languages | Cross-host numeric & `data/float64?` suite: boxed `1.0` (`2.0 + 1.0`, `inc(1.0)`), `2 ** -3`, negative/nonfinite `%` operands, fractional `**` refusal, collections containing `-0.0` & `NaN` (`[0.0] == [-0.0]`, `[NaN] == [NaN]`, `{\"a\": -0.0} == {\"a\": 0.0}`); entry normal return value (`20` preserved) + callee binding errors delivered under `:yang.call/thrown`; `clj.py/call` rejecting forged `{:yang.call/entry ...}` maps before `yang.call/invoke`; dynamic `comp`/`partial` closures called from independently compiled `clj.py`/`yang.clojure`/`py`/`js`/`php` units preserving identity; lexical shadowing of projected names (`conj`, `is_empty`, `map`) leaving lowered UAST uncaptured; primitive callable projections (`filter(is_empty, ...)`); per-module `globals` isolation across two units; `[:yin.k/ok 42]` ordinary data returned unstripped; condition-shaped user throws vs. retained protocol exceptions (`A→B→A` `finally` cleanup); portable `clojure.core` subset excluding `var?`/`resolve`; 4-host execution parity. |\n   701\t| **P4 — Tier-2 shared modules (`yrt.gen`, `yrt.safepoint`)** | Extract parameterized `yrt.gen` (preserving Python `:base` rebasing vs. PHP direct context restoration and refcount cleanup) and `yrt.safepoint` (`stream/poll!` skeleton for `pysp`/`jssp`). | **One bump** (deferred) | Generator + safepoint parity suites across VMs/hosts, preserving PHP lifecycle/cleanup policy and non-rebasing context behavior vs. Python rebasing. |\n   702\t\n   703\t---\n   704\t\n   705\t## 10. Open owner decisions\n   706\t\n   707\t1. **D1 — Local mutation model for `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`:**\n   708\t   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* `:mutation/locals :cell` (task-heap cells holding pure persistent Clojure values, matching Python parameter binding, unbound reads, reassignment, loops, and `nonlocal` with per-module `globals` cells). Keep `:single-assignment` as a separate restricted profile.\n   709\t   - *Option B:* `:mutation/locals :single-assignment` only (refuses local reassignment).\n   710\t2. **D2 — Namespace prefix for Layer-2a shared modules:**\n   711\t   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* `yrt.*` (`yrt.escape`, `yrt.float`, `yrt.int`, `yrt.gen`, `yrt.safepoint`) matching `yang.typescript.md` §17 and `yang.php.md` §9, implemented in Clojure under `src/cljc/yang/rt/*.cljc`.\n   712\t   - *Option B:* `yang.rt.*` for both Clojure namespaces and linker module names.\n   713\t3. **D3 — Python float tagging during P1:**\n   714\t   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* Retain `{:py/float x}` behind a 2-line `py` boundary adapter around `yrt.float` so P1 stays a pure runtime extraction without shifting Python value semantics or equality.\n   715\t   - *Option B:* Migrate Python to untagged `data/float64` carriers in P1.\n   716\t4. **D4 — Batching P1 (`yrt.escape` + `yrt.float` + `yrt.int`) vs. per-module bumps:**\n   717\t   - *Option A (Recommended conditionally — Architect concurred):* Implement and test each `yrt.*` extraction independently first, then activate all three in one coordinated profile bump so `:segment/blake3-*` goldens refresh once.\n   718\t   - *Option B:* Ship each `yrt.*` module as a separate profile bump.\n   719\t5. **D5 — Cross-syntax identifier mapping for Clojure names (`?`, `!`, `-`):**\n   720\t   - *Option A (Recommended — Architect concurred):* Curated `:yang.semantics/ambient-projections` table validated against exact exports, lexical precedence, primitive callable projections, and reserved-door bans.\n   721\t   - *Option B:* Algorithmic mangling rule (`_q` / `_bang`).\n   722\t6. **D6 — Publishing `clojure.core` as a standalone linked module:**\n   723\t   - *Option A (Constrained, Recommended — Architect concurred):* Publish the portable `clojure.core` subset (`§7.5`) with per-task instantiation in P3 for `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` and future profiles, while keeping `yang.clojure`'s default `library-for` bundling unchanged in P3 (migrating `yang.clojure` separately later so P3 moves zero Clojure goldens).\n   724\t   - *Option B:* Copy needed `library` definitions into `clj.py`.\n   725\t7. **D7 — Float exponentiation rounding (`py`/`js` half-power vs. `php` base squaring):**\n   726\t   - *Option A (Recommended for P1):* Export both `yrt.float/fpow-half` and `yrt.float/fpow-base` so P1 preserves bit-exact parity (`1.1 ** 6`: `0x1.c585058dde7acp+0` for `py`/`js` vs `0x1.c585058dde7abp+0` for `php`) across all existing oracles.\n   727\t   - *Option B:* Explicitly approve unifying PHP onto `fpow-half` (or `py`/`js` onto `fpow-base`) and update the affected language's oracle departure ledger.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
