{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'authentic\\\\?|:cell/authentic' src/cljc/yin/vm | head -65\"","aggregated_output":"src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:2804:          :cell/authentic?\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:388:;; module publishes `authentic?`, the ruling-of-record query a caller's\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:414:  (make-effect :cell/authentic? {:cell c}))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:441:  {'new new-cell, 'get get-cell, 'set! set-cell!, 'authentic? authentic-cell?,\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:452:   'authentic? (vm/primitive-profile 'authentic? :effectful [1]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc:453:                                     #{:cell/authentic?} :none)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/docs/ast.md:678:Runtime-allocated mutable locations are not AST nodes. They are the `cell` host module's `cell/new`, `cell/get`, `cell/set!` and `cell/authentic?`, ordinary applications whose effects the engine interprets on all four VMs. `cell/new` answers a sealed `{:type :cell-ref :id :cell-N :seal s}`; the content lives in the task's `:heap` (see `state.md`), never in the named store. `cell/authentic?` is the ruling-of-record pure query (yang.antlr.md 8.10.12): the heap's own yes-or-no on a candidate reference, answered as data where `cell/get` would fail closed.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
