{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_41","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc | sed -n '2454,2525p;2550,2577p'\"","aggregated_output":"  2454\t           ;; The exception accessors and the continuation family. The\n  2455\t           ;; `dsg__ex_message`/`dsg__ex_data` accessors read the portable\n  2456\t           ;; ex-info map; the continuation family (`clj/try`, `clj/throw`,\n  2457\t           ;; `clj/raise`, ...) is the port's `%capture` handler-stack scheme,\n  2458\t           ;; emitted inline (the linked runtime binds the same family from the\n  2459\t           ;; prelude). Its capture-sensitive primitives are the `dsg__*`\n  2460\t           ;; names bound outside it.\n  2461\t           (outcomes? env) (u/let1 'dsg__ex_message\n  2462\t                                   (u/sexp->uast ex-message-form))\n  2463\t           (outcomes? env) (u/let1 'dsg__ex_data\n  2464\t                                   (u/sexp->uast ex-data-form))\n  2465\t           ;; A linked unit shares the required clj module's handler stack.\n  2466\t           ;; Its inline counterpart names the private clj.rt/ctx store key,\n  2467\t           ;; which cannot be read from a different module.\n  2468\t           (and (outcomes? env) (not (:linked-runtime opts))) (u/then\n  2469\t                                                                (discard-result continuation-uast))\n  2470\t           (outcomes? env) (u/then\n  2471\t                             (discard-result\n  2472\t                               (u/app (u/lam '[get = assoc empty?] call/uast)\n  2473\t                                      (u/v 'dsg__get) (u/v 'dsg__equal)\n  2474\t                                      (u/v 'dsg__assoc) (u/v 'dsg__empty))))\n  2475\t           (outcomes? env) (u/let1 'dsg__call_token (u/lam [] (u/lit nil)))\n  2476\t           ;; Guest closures keep captured environments portable: binding host\n  2477\t           ;; primitive values here would make UCF machine-data validation fail.\n  2478\t           ;; These helpers cover generated map lookups/writes and comparisons;\n  2479\t           ;; conj/vec are already protected by the convention's binder checks.\n  2480\t           ;; Evaluate siblings outside each other's bindings to avoid retaining\n  2481\t           ;; a chain of redundant helper environments.\n  2482\t           (outcomes? env) (#(u/app\n  2483\t                               (u/lam '[dsg__get dsg__equal dsg__assoc dsg__empty] %)\n  2484\t                               (if (contains? (::defined env) 'get)\n  2485\t                                 (u/sexp->uast\n  2486\t                                   '(fn [m k]\n  2487\t                                      (if (data/map? m)\n  2488\t                                        (let [find (fn [self entries]\n  2489\t                                                     (if (data/content= 0 (data/count entries))\n  2490\t                                                       nil\n  2491\t                                                       (let [pair (data/nth entries 0)]\n  2492\t                                                         (if (data/content= k (data/nth pair 0))\n  2493\t                                                           (data/nth pair 1)\n  2494\t                                                           (self self (data/subvec entries 1))))))]\n  2495\t                                          (find find (vec m)))\n  2496\t                                        nil)))\n  2497\t                                 (u/sexp->uast '(fn [m k] (get m k))))\n  2498\t                               (u/sexp->uast '(fn [a b] (data/content= a b)))\n  2499\t                               (if (contains? (::defined env) 'assoc)\n  2500\t                                 (u/sexp->uast\n  2501\t                                   '(fn [m k v k2 v2 k3 v3]\n  2502\t                                      (let [one (conj m (conj [] k v))]\n  2503\t                                        (if (data/content= k2 nil)\n  2504\t                                          one\n  2505\t                                          (let [two (conj one (conj [] k2 v2))]\n  2506\t                                            (if (data/content= k3 nil)\n  2507\t                                              two\n  2508\t                                              (conj two (conj [] k3 v3))))))))\n  2509\t                                 (u/sexp->uast\n  2510\t                                   '(fn [m k v k2 v2 k3 v3]\n  2511\t                                      (if (data/content= k2 nil)\n  2512\t                                        (assoc m k v)\n  2513\t                                        (if (data/content= k3 nil)\n  2514\t                                          (assoc m k v k2 v2)\n  2515\t                                          (assoc m k v k2 v2 k3 v3))))))\n  2516\t                               (u/sexp->uast '(fn [xs] (data/content= 0 (data/count xs))))))\n  2517\t           (outcomes? env) tails/remark-tails))))))\n  2518\t\n  2519\t\n  2520\t;; =============================================================================\n  2521\t;; The guest collection and higher-order library (slice 7)\n  2522\t;; =============================================================================\n  2523\t;;\n  2524\t;; Guest-side source, compiled through this compiler like any program: the\n  2525\t;; functions that invoke guest closures (map, filter, reduce, comp, partial)\n  2550\t;; Known compromises: `reduced` is an untyped tagged map, so reduced? matches\n  2551\t;; any map holding :yin.k/reduced true; seq refuses a non-collection (a string\n  2552\t;; is the data module's str-* ops, not a seq); eager sequences are lists;\n  2553\t;; rem rejects non-integers and a zero divisor before arithmetic; the compiler\n  2554\t;; emits bare conj and vec, so a program may not define or bind either.\n  2555\t;; When collection calls are needed, invoke-value is a library helper whose\n  2556\t;; local capture is refused explicitly.\n  2557\t;;\n  2558\t;; Variadic Clojure functions are fixed-arity here (the convention has no\n  2559\t;; variadic parameter): str, list and vector admit 0 to 6 arguments, concat and\n  2560\t;; merge 0 to 4, union 0 to 6, difference 2, comp 0 to 3, partial binds 1 to 3.\n  2561\t;; A larger count is the\n  2562\t;; function's own arity error.\n  2563\t\n  2564\t(def library-adapters\n  2565\t  \"The retired `:adapters` map a program using `library` once compiled with:\n  2566\t   the data exports whose refusal the collection predicates read as data.\n  2567\t   The continuation port rewrote those predicates onto the `data/*` and\n  2568\t   `kind/*` host predicates, so no `portable/*` adapter is consulted; the\n  2569\t   map stays for the `library-opts`/`unit-opts` fixtures and the prelude's\n  2570\t   `admit` registration.\"\n  2571\t  {'data/count 'portable/count\n  2572\t   'data/peek 'portable/peek\n  2573\t   'data/dissoc 'portable/dissoc\n  2574\t   'data/disj 'portable/disj\n  2575\t   'data/str-length 'portable/str-length})\n  2576\t\n  2577\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
