{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_58","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.antlr.md | sed -n '3640,3780p'\"","aggregated_output":"  3640\tCross-language passage must not allocate a replacement function cell.\n  3641\tReturned functions retain their original identity, captures, defaults,\n  3642\tbound receiver, properties, and static state. A receiving frontend's\n  3643\tcallable test follows this common eligibility rule rather than rejecting\n  3644\tforeign native tags. Foreign attribute access and type reflection remain\n  3645\tprofile-owned; callability grants no general right to interpret another\n  3646\truntime's cell layout.\n  3647\t\n  3648\tCompiler-internal lambdas and host functions do not acquire this\n  3649\tconvention merely by being applicable in Yin. A source import exposing\n  3650\tone must emit an entry from its declared signature and effect profile.\n  3651\tIt must not guess an opaque closure's signature or bypass host-effect\n  3652\tand custody rules. Internal helper calls need not construct records.\n  3653\t\n  3654\t#### 8.10.3 Invocation record\n  3655\t\n  3656\tThe invocation is an ephemeral in-machine value. These keys are proposed\n  3657\tvocabulary, not existing repository APIs:\n  3658\t\n  3659\t```clojure\n  3660\t{:yang.call/callee     f\n  3661\t :yang.call/positional [v0 v1 ...]\n  3662\t :yang.call/named      [[\"name\" value] ...]\n  3663\t :yang.call/raise      raise-exit\n  3664\t ;; Optional: presence means a receiver was supplied, even when nil.\n  3665\t :yang.call/receiver   receiver\n  3666\t ;; Optional: pinned argument-binding extension, for example locations.\n  3667\t :yang.call/binding-profile \"<content-address>\"}\n  3668\t```\n  3669\t\n  3670\tThe four required fields mean:\n  3671\t\n  3672\t- `:yang.call/callee`: the original resolved callable, including its\n  3673\t  identity. The invocation helper supplies it; an extracted entry must\n  3674\t  not be applied to another object's substituted state.\n  3675\t- `:yang.call/positional`: a dense ordered vector of evaluated values.\n  3676\t  Its length records presence; no missing-argument sentinel is inserted.\n  3677\t- `:yang.call/named`: ordered name/value pairs, not a map. Names are\n  3678\t  plain text without caller-side case folding or normalization.\n  3679\t  Duplicate names remain visible until the callee's binder decides them.\n  3680\t- `:yang.call/raise`: this activation's caller-supplied, non-returning\n  3681\t  guest exit, accepting the condition in section 8.10.7. It closes over\n  3682\t  the caller's continuation and exception machinery, never a host\n  3683\t  callback or hidden global handler slot.\n  3684\t\n  3685\tAn absent receiver differs from one whose value is `nil`, `:py/None`,\n  3686\t`:php/null`, `:js/null`, or `:js/undefined`. Empty argument vectors are\n  3687\trequired rather than represented by absent keys. Presence must not be\n  3688\tinferred from truthiness.\n  3689\t\n  3690\tThe optional binding profile pins additional argument semantics. It\n  3691\tdoes not name the caller's language or select a language-pair bridge.\n  3692\tAbsent that extension, arguments are by-value runtime values as in\n  3693\tsection 8.10.6. The callee entry compares the supplied profile address\n  3694\twith its declared accepted/required binding profiles before acquiring\n  3695\treferences or entering the body. An unsupported required profile or a\n  3696\tmissing required extension fails there. The pinned profile defines the\n  3697\tshape and validation of any extra invocation fields it requires; values\n  3698\tin the base vectors alone do not establish a location protocol.\n  3699\t\n  3700\tThe PHP reference-argument profile is pinned as\n  3701\t`sha256:171656777d777865312132fe18cbc7a057a4721844a4dc450c0800381d2223eb`.\n  3702\tPHP call sites include it when their declared target has reference\n  3703\tparameters; corresponding positional values may then be PHP reference\n  3704\tmarkers for caller locations. The PHP entry rejects unknown profile\n  3705\taddresses before parameter binding, and only this profile authorizes its\n  3706\tbinder to attach a parameter to a caller marker. The markers alone carry\n  3707\tno binding authority.\n  3708\t\n  3709\tConvention revision is pinned by the existing lowering/runtime profiles.\n  3710\tIt is not a new canonical AST slot, a per-function language tag, or a\n  3711\trepeated version field in every invocation. Incompatible revisions need\n  3712\tnew profiles and explicit admission, never entry-shape guessing.\n  3713\t\n  3714\tThe shared helper validates the record's map shape, required presence,\n  3715\tpositional vector, and ordered pairs with text names. The callee entry\n  3716\tvalidates extension fields under its admitted binding profile; the shared\n  3717\thelper knows no extension-specific representation. A valid caller-owned\n  3718\traise exit is established before constructing the record, so structural\n  3719\tfailures can be transferred through it. If no valid raise exit exists,\n  3720\tthat is an operational wiring failure; do not invent a source exception\n  3721\tpath, default missing fields to `nil`, or broadly catch VM application\n  3722\terrors. Checking live entry/exit/predicate closure arity is not part of\n  3723\tthis validation; constructor fixtures and admission under pinned\n  3724\tprofiles establish those obligations.\n  3725\t\n  3726\t#### 8.10.4 Source semantics at caller and callee\n  3727\t\n  3728\tThe caller's lowering preserves its source rules for callable resolution,\n  3729\targument/receiver evaluation, and spread or unpacking. Evaluate each\n  3730\texpression exactly once, in the source-defined order. Errors required\n  3731\tbefore argument evaluation must still occur before it. The record holds\n  3732\tevaluated values; the callee must not reevaluate source expressions.\n  3733\t\n  3734\tAfter source resolution, calls use the common projection and application.\n  3735\tFor a cell-backed callable, the successful path is schematically:\n  3736\t\n  3737\t```clojure\n  3738\t;; UAST notation after source evaluation/resolution and validation.\n  3739\t;; The caller has already established `raise-exit`.\n  3740\t(let [entry (get (cell/get f) :yang.call/entry)\n  3741\t      invocation (assoc evaluated-arguments\n  3742\t                        :yang.call/callee f\n  3743\t                        :yang.call/raise raise-exit)]\n  3744\t  (entry invocation))\n  3745\t```\n  3746\t\n  3747\tThe shared prelude handles projection and validation for cell-backed and\n  3748\timmutable callables. Existing `py/call`, `js/call`, or `php/call` names\n  3749\tmay remain as source call-site helpers, but must not reject an admitted\n  3750\tforeign callable because its native type tag differs.\n  3751\t\n  3752\tThe callee entry installs its exception boundary **before parameter\n  3753\tbinding**. It owns defaults, arity checks, positional/named/variadic\n  3754\tbinding, receiver interpretation, and supported source constraints and\n  3755\tcoercions. It then invokes its body using its private lowered signature\n  3756\tand captured environment.\n  3757\t\n  3758\tEntry boilerplate is not an additional source function activation.\n  3759\tSource recursion limits, tracing, and safepoint call marks must count the\n  3760\toriginal source activation once, not both the entry and its private body\n  3761\tas two source calls. Genuine nested source calls remain observable.\n  3762\t\n  3763\t| Callee example | Interpretation of the same invocation |\n  3764\t|---|---|\n  3765\t| Python function | Python binding/default/keyword rules and captured module globals. A missing required argument raises the Python binding error. |\n  3766\t| JavaScript function | Its receiver mode and argument/default/rest rules. An absent argument yields `undefined` where specified. Nonempty named arguments raise a guest `TypeError`; they are not discarded or converted to a positional object. |\n  3767\t| PHP function | Named-parameter, static-state, reference and declared type rules. Function self comes from `:yang.call/callee`, not the JavaScript receiver. |\n  3768\t| Further frontend | Its declared binding rules, with no new case in the shared prelude or evaluator. |\n  3769\t\n  3770\tA Python unbound function does not gain a first positional argument\n  3771\tbecause a JavaScript member call supplied a receiver. A bound-method entry\n  3772\tsupplies its already-bound self once. An arrow entry retains lexical\n  3773\t`this`. Callables that do not use a receiver ignore its presence.\n  3774\t\n  3775\tSource callable objects perform dynamic target lookup in their entry\n  3776\twhen required. Entry publication must not freeze a target whose meaning\n  3777\tmay change under supported source operations. Callability does not alter\n  3778\tname lookup or introduce fallback to another language's globals.\n  3779\t\n  3780\t#### 8.10.5 Values and projections\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
