{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.antlr.md | sed -n '3153,3179p;4104,4142p;4325,4363p'\"","aggregated_output":"  3153\t+-----------+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n  3154\t```\n  3155\t\n  3156\tThe REPL `__main__` persists across submissions (ruling 18): its module\n  3157\tobject, globals dict, builtin namespace, and import cache. `(reset)` is a\n  3158\tnew Python process: fresh task-owned runtime state, handler stacks and\n  3159\thook attachments included, while immutable verified code may be reused.\n  3160\tRuntime state never merges across frontend revisions, and late results\n  3161\tfrom the old process cannot mutate the new one.\n  3162\t\n  3163\tForeign-principal imports are not claimed until D7 slice B lands with\n  3164\tits tests (ruling 19), verifying closure origin and store ownership\n  3165\trecursively through exports, re-exports, and transitive dependency\n  3166\tslices before any executable value is exposed. B is necessary, not\n  3167\tsufficient: the claim also needs authenticated publication,\n  3168\tdependency-pin checks, primitive and effect admission, and working\n  3169\tstore-context transitions on all four VMs. Until B lands, a forged\n  3170\t`:store-of` could reach the prelude's state. Corrected float publication\n  3171\trebuilds affected derivations, manifests, and dependency pins before any\n  3172\tcross-principal address is accepted. Trust is a separate question:\n  3173\twhich principals' modules a holder admits is the linker's admission\n  3174\t(`yin.vm.linker.dht.md` section 7.5, slices AL-1 to AL-4), which is\n  3175\tlanguage-blind and the same for every frontend, and an allow never\n  3176\trelaxes this check.\n  3177\t\n  3178\tLinker prerequisites, the linker seat's to build:\n  3179\t\n  4104\t  decision remains in compiled guest code).\n  4105\t- **Routing asks the heap, never the shape.**