{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_85","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc | sed -n '1046,1102p'\"","aggregated_output":"  1046\t  [encode store]\n  1047\t  (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(encode k) (encode v)])) store))\n  1048\t\n  1049\t\n  1050\t(defn- decode-store\n  1051\t  [decode snapshot]\n  1052\t  (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(decode k) (decode v)])) snapshot))\n  1053\t\n  1054\t\n  1055\t(defn lift-slice\n  1056\t  \"Act 1 of `linked` (yin.vm.linker.md section 7.3): the halted child's\n  1057\t   exports and module stores in the portable encoding. `own` is the\n  1058\t   module's manifest address. Returns `{:slice {sym encoded} :stores\n  1059\t   {address snapshot} :cells {cell-id cell} :origins #{segment}}`: one\n  1060\t   snapshot per module -- the child's own store under `own`, and every\n  1061\t   dependency store the encoding reaches as it stands in the child at\n  1062\t   halt, mutations included -- and the logical cursor cells the encoded\n  1063\t   references name. A `:store-of` with no snapshot is\n  1064\t   `:yin.k/non-portable` of kind `:missing-module-store`; any refused leaf\n  1065\t   refuses the lift.\"\n  1066\t  [child own exports]\n  1067\t  (let [found (atom {:origins #{}, :stores #{}, :cells {}, :cell-of {}})\n  1068\t        encode (encoder child own found)\n  1069\t        store (:store child)\n  1070\t        slice (into {} (map (fn [k] [k (encode (get store k))])) exports)\n  1071\t        stores (loop [stores {own (encode-store encode store)}]\n  1072\t                 (let [pending (remove #(contains? stores %)\n  1073\t                                       (sort-by str (:stores @found)))]\n  1074\t                   (if (empty? pending)\n  1075\t                     stores\n  1076\t                     (recur\n  1077\t                       (reduce\n  1078\t                         (fn [acc m]\n  1079\t                           (if-let [s (get-in child [:module-stores m])]\n  1080\t                             (assoc acc m (encode-store encode s))\n  1081\t                             (non-portable! :missing-module-store\n  1082\t                                            {store-of-key m})))\n  1083\t                         stores\n  1084\t                         pending)))))]\n  1085\t    {:slice slice,\n  1086\t     :stores stores,\n  1087\t     :cells (:cells @found),\n  1088\t     :origins (:origins @found)}))\n  1089\t\n  1090\t\n  1091\t(defn receive-module\n  1092\t  \"Acts 3 and 4 of `linked` for one receiving task (yin.vm.linker.md\n  1093\t   section 7.3): attach every origin image of `entry` the kernel does not\n  1094\t   yet hold, non-destructively; lower the resources the slice and the\n  1095\t   snapshots it instantiates reference into the task's private\n  1096\t   `:resources` (r9); lower the slice against this task's own\n  1097\t   coordinates into the entry's `:bindings`, every reference re-sealed\n  1098\t   under this task's secret (r10); and instantiate each store snapshot\n  1099\t   into `:module-stores` unless the task already holds that module's\n  1100\t   store -- first link wins, a live instance is never overwritten.\n  1101\t   Nothing is written into the task's own `:store`. A registry pin\n  1102\t   conflict throws its refusal data before any attachment or lowering.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_86","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'node\\\\?|not-callable|admiss' docs/design/yang.preludes.md | tail -18\"","aggregated_output":"229:  - **Context policy difference (`py` vs. `php`):** In live code, `py/gen-enter` (`yang.python.antlr.prelude:457–458`) and `py/gen-start` (`:470`) compute a rebased `:base = (+ 1 (abs-depth caller-ctx))`, whereas `php/gen-start` (`yang.php.antlr.prelude:5311`) starts at `(php/ctx nil 0 0 nil)` and `php/gen-enter` (`:5305`) restores `(get s :ctx)` directly without rebasing. `yrt.gen` therefore accepts explicit `on-start-ctx` and `on-resume-ctx` policy closures alongside `on-enter`, `on-exit`, `on-fail`, and `on-throw-closed`, keeping PHP's refcount/cleanup lifecycle (`cleanup`, `addref`/`release`) and Python's `RecursionError` admission checks strictly language-owned.\n234:## 5. Declarative prelude composition, recipes, and admission\n241:   Used by `yang.core.prelude` + `yang.core.prelude-admission` to produce the module's UAST, schema-1 manifest, and C1 side table from the owning language's definition list.\n287:### 5.2 Composition rules and verified-closure admission\n289:`yang.core.prelude` and `yang.core.prelude-admission` enforce six fail-closed checks:\n300:   - Rather than duplicating the manifest's derived effect set (honoring \"Derive, don't persist\"), `:yang.prelude/max-effects` is strictly optional. When present, admission checks `(clojure.set/subset? derived-transitive-effects max-effects)` and refuses if any transitive module or host declaration exceeds the ceiling.\n301:5. **Host-module and limit admission (`admit-profile`):**\n302:   - Verifies that `registry` supplies every required host export (`prelude-admission/admit`) and meets every numeric/data floor (`:min-bits`, `:min-digits`, `:min-max-items`) before any unit publishes or runs.\n464:     3. **`:yang.semantics/ambient-projections`** (resolved via `clj.py/global-get` fallback to the module's explicit projected lookup map, or refused at runtime/admission if absent).\n499:This section specifies the reference cross-paradigm profile in full, reconciling Python's lowering ABI, 4-host numeric portability, cross-unit callable admission, §8.10.7 exception bridging, and a portable `clojure.core` module.\n585:### 7.4 Cross-unit callable admission, source authority, and §8.10.7 exception bridging\n587:Because `yang.call/eligible?` (`src/cljc/yang/core/call.cljc:29–48`) only dereferences authenticated cell-refs and leaves ordinary maps intact, structural eligibility alone does **not** stop source-constructed maps carrying `:yang.call/entry` from masquerading as callables when source maps are first-class data. Likewise, as `src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1280–1306` and `2400–2424` show, immutable Clojure descriptors carry a unit-local `:clj/admission` witness closing over that unit's private `dsg__call_token` rather than cross-unit admission, whereas **authenticated task-heap cells** (`cell/authentic?`, `clojure.cljc:2400–2408`) are admitted across **every** independently compiled unit (`yang.clojure`, `clojure.core`, `clj.py`, `py`, `js`, `php`).\n591:1. **Source-level callable admission (`clj.py/admitted-callable?`):**\n600:   - Any plain source map (including `{:yang.call/entry ...}`) or unauthenticated `{:type :cell-ref ...}` map fails `clj.py/admitted-callable?` immediately; `clj.py/call` mints a retained `:yang.call/not-callable` protocol condition via private `cell/dsg__new-provenance` and raises it via `clj/raise`, never calling `yang.call/invoke` on forged source data.\n628:     - `fn?`: checks `clj.py`-equivalent authenticated cell admission (`(and (data/map? x) (= (get x :type) :cell-ref) (cell/authentic? x) (data/callable? (yang.call/entry x)) (yang.call/eligible? x))`, or `(data/callable? x)` only for primitive/VM closures, never plain maps).\n637:     - Dynamic calls to user-supplied closures (`f` in `map`, `filter`, `remove`, `reduce`, `update`, `comp`, `partial`) go through standalone `clojure.core`'s dynamic call helper, which validates authenticated cell admission (`cell/authentic?` + `data/callable?` entry + `yang.call/eligible?`) and invokes `yang.call/invoke` with the §8.10.7 exception bridge — **never** using `yang.clojure`'s map-only `[dsg__call_token args]` shortcut (`clojure.cljc:2432`). Returned closures from `comp`/`partial` keep identical cell identity across every independently compiled frontend unit with zero receiver-side replacement wrappers.\n678:Layer C (Registry Admission):    yang.core.prelude-admission, yang.core.module, yang.core.publication\n697:| **P0 — Composition plumbing & `defquoted` consolidation** | Consolidate `defquoted` into `yang.core.prelude`; implement `:yang.prelude/recipe` / `:yang.prelude/profile` composition and verified-closure validation in `yang.core.prelude` + `prelude-admission` (preserving operand sequencing, `init!` placement, tail marking, `:linear`/`:balanced` mode, and Clojure's custom preamble). | **Zero** (byte-identical emission) | Compare generated UAST/specs against frozen pre-change snapshots of `py`/`js`/`php`/`clj`/`yang.call`; test verified-closure edge validation, missing transitive artifact/export refusal, provenance-door/effect-ceiling exclusions, and projected-name collision refusal. |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
