{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_87","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/yang.antlr.md | sed -n '3946,3976p;269,297p'\"","aggregated_output":"   269\t## 3. Language frontend SPI\n   270\t\n   271\t### 3.1 Portable declarations versus installed implementations\n   272\t\n   273\tA frontend consists of four independently versioned parts:\n   274\t\n   275\t1. **Grammar package:** lexer/parser grammars, imports, token vocabulary,\n   276\t   entry rules, and required parsing helpers.\n   277\t2. **Syntax export profile:** how the generated parser's CST becomes\n   278\t   portable data.\n   279\t3. **Semantic frontend:** scope analysis, validation, desugaring, and\n   280\t   Universal AST lowering.\n   281\t4. **Runtime profile:** prelude code, value representations, calling\n   282\t   convention, primitive requirements, and permitted effects.\n   283\t\n   284\tA proposed portable manifest might contain:\n   285\t\n   286\t```clojure\n   287\t{:yang.frontend/id :example.ruby/frontend\n   288\t :yang.frontend/spi 1\n   289\t :yang.frontend/revision \"<immutable-package-revision>\"\n   290\t :yang.frontend/language :example.ruby/language\n   291\t\n   292\t :yang.frontend/grammar\n   293\t {:yang.grammar/package \"<content-address>\"\n   294\t  :yang.grammar/lexer \"RubyLexer\"\n   295\t  :yang.grammar/parser \"RubyParser\"\n   296\t  :yang.grammar/entries\n   297\t  {:module \"program\"\n  3946\t#### 8.10.9 Publication, visibility, and reproducibility\n  3947\t\n  3948\tShared callability creates no common global scope. An import or\n  3949\tcomposition explicitly binds exports in the receiving source namespace\n  3950\tunder its normal name/module rules. Missing names keep their source\n  3951\terrors. No fallback searches other frontends, the filesystem, a host\n  3952\tpackage registry, or ambient globals.\n  3953\t\n  3954\tLinked modules publish code and immutable specifications. Their bodies\n  3955\tinstantiate function objects and common entries in the importing task,\n  3956\tas section 8.5.6 requires. Install children must not export live function\n  3957\tcells. A higher-order result is an ordinary runtime value, not a new\n  3958\tlinker publication on each call.\n  3959\t\n  3960\tLowering/runtime profiles pin the implementation and binding/value\n  3961\textensions. Existing dependency/effect/custody checks remain. Type facts\n  3962\tstay beside code under `yin.vm.typecheck`, not in lambda language tags.\n  3963\tDo not duplicate existing lambda parameters in another persisted\n  3964\tauthority over the private body signature.\n  3965\t\n  3966\tBefore admitting a compiled composition, its profile/dependency\n  3967\tdeclarations must establish one compatible convention revision for the\n  3968\tentries it exposes. An incompatible revision needs an explicitly pinned\n  3969\tprojection or is refused before execution. Neither a common slot name nor\n  3970\tan opaque runtime closure proves revision compatibility. No runtime\n  3971\tlanguage registry or inspection of captured environments supplies it.\n  3972\t\n  3973\tChanged entry code changes code identities through the normal encoder.\n  3974\tRetain source, lowered UAST, pinned profiles, and projections under\n  3975\texisting provenance/unitarity rules. A fast path may omit the record\n  3976\tonly after proving equivalent evaluation, binding, foreign callability,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
